# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   For an app, this is usually fine to prevent policies from colliding.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1263, we should share the Pipfile.lock.
#   However, if you're working on a library, not an app, you may choose to ignore it.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock is optionally ignored.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock is optionally ignored.
#pdm.lock

